============================================================
Step 5: Physical interpretation of generators
============================================================
  Each generator is a direction in log-space along which
  the friction factor f is preserved. Physically: a
  simultaneous rescaling of variables that keeps the flow
  invariant (Darcy/Forchheimer regime preserved).

  Generator 1:
    dP_L x exp(+0.427*eps), v x exp(+0.830*eps), mu x exp(+0.075*eps), d x exp(-0.066*eps), phi x exp(-0.346*eps)
    Meaning: increase v while increase dP_L, increase mu, decrease d, decrease phi
             to keep friction factor f invariant

  Generator 2:
    dP_L x exp(-0.187*eps), v x exp(+0.075*eps), mu x exp(+0.967*eps), phi x exp(+0.152*eps)
    Meaning: increase mu while decrease dP_L, increase v, increase phi
             to keep friction factor f invariant

  Generator 3:
    rho x exp(+1.000*eps)

  Generator 4:
    dP_L x exp(+0.166*eps), v x exp(-0.066*eps), d x exp(+0.974*eps), phi x exp(-0.134*eps)
    Meaning: increase d while increase dP_L, decrease v, decrease phi
             to keep friction factor f invariant

  Generator 5:
    dP_L x exp(+0.866*eps), v x exp(-0.346*eps), mu x exp(+0.152*eps), d x exp(-0.134*eps), phi x exp(+0.298*eps)
    Meaning: increase dP_L while decrease v, increase mu, decrease d, increase phi
             to keep friction factor f invariant


